WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
A number on its own tells you nothing.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.070
Say a length is 3.0.

3
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.300
Is that tiny, or huge?

4
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.440
No unit, no meaning.

5
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:13.810
So every quantity in physics
is a number times a unit.

6
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.660
Force comes in newtons.

7
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.310
Energy in joules.

8
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.040
Power in watts.

9
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:22.200
They sound like three
separate, basic units.

10
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.470
So what is a newton actually made of?

11
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.210
A joule?

12
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.390
A watt?

13
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.510
In this mission, you'll meet
the six base units of the SI,

14
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.070
and the seventh you won't need.

15
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.790
Then you'll work through the
prefixes, from tera down to pico,

16
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.130
and find the trap in squaring them.

17
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: find out what each of
these three units is really made of.
